From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Harfouche <mark.harfouche@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Sep 2026 14:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Dispatch multi-animal TensorFlow training on the pose engine

core/train_multianimal.py was the only TensorFlow entry point that never
consulted nnets.factory.resolve_engine.  It built the Keras net
unconditionally, with PoseNetFactory.create(cfg, engine=KERAS_ENGINE), and
called ensure_eager_execution(), so neither `tf_engine: tf1` in pose_cfg.yaml
nor DLC_TF_ENGINE=tf1 could reach the graph-mode loop -- and
0018-Port-the-multi-animal-training-loop-to-eager-Tensor.patch had deleted
that loop, leaving core/legacy_tf1.py with only the single-animal train().
tf1 being the default engine therefore protected nobody with a multi-animal
project.

Any process that evaluated or analysed before it (re)trained died at the next
train_network with

    RuntimeError: The Keras pose nets need eager execution, but this process
    has already built a TF1 graph.

because prediction had entered graph mode first and TF1 ops already existed.
That is the order the GUI works in and the order SpatiotemporalAdaptation's
own docstring prescribes; examples/testscript_tensorflow_multi_animal.py does
it too and stopped at its second train_network call.

The DeepLabCut 3.0.1 multi-animal loop moves into core/legacy_tf1.py, beside
the single-animal one already there, unchanged apart from its prologue.
train() becomes the dispatcher core/train.py already is: it chdirs, sets
logging up, reads and adjusts the config once, and hands the result to
whichever loop resolve_engine picks.  The eager loop keeps every line it had
and is still reached with `tf_engine: keras` or DLC_TF_ENGINE=keras.

Reading the config in the caller also keeps setup_logging() ahead of the
first logging call for both loops -- config.cfg_from_file() logs -- and the
return to the original directory now happens in a finally.

examples/testscript_tensorflow_multi_animal.py, NET pinned to dlcrnet_ms5,
reaches "ALL DONE!!! - default multianimal cases are functional." again, both
with the default engine and with DLC_TF_ENGINE=keras.
---
 .../core/legacy_tf1.py                        | 192 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../core/train_multianimal.py                 | 140 +++++++++----
 2 files changed, 290 insertions(+), 42 deletions(-)

